{"authored" [{"question" "q-114415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2}){e}^{x},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=0$\n- ${f}^{″}(0)>0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2}){e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{x}+(-1+2x){e}^{x}=({x}^{2}+x){e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+x){e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ x(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-1,0.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=({x}^{2}+x)\\cdot {e}^{x}+(2x+1){e}^{x}=({x}^{2}+3x+1){e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =-{e}^{-1}<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =1>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I and II are true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so there is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statements III is false. $x=1$ is not a critical point.\n\n- Statement IV is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and IV only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "62bff426ce2a3d3733958909ae26160db95e94c280c7f7746696465f5547d25c" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and IV only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x) = x^3-6x^2-15x.$ Given that $f'(5) = 0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f''(5)  >           0$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=5$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=5$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/example-3744.json" "file_sha256" "ee17bd7030b3b511f10fe17bb2baaf4f385d32e8236cf6b0a1746ad20b833d84" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $x=5$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=  x^3-6x^2-15x,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x) =  3x^2-12x-15\n$$\n\nWe're given that $f'(5) = 0.$ Indeed, we can see that $f'(5) = 3(5)^2 - 12(5) - 15 = 0.$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =6x-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(5) & =6(5)-12 \\\\  & =30-12 \\\\  & =18>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/example-3744.json" "file_sha256" "ee17bd7030b3b511f10fe17bb2baaf4f385d32e8236cf6b0a1746ad20b833d84" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the $x$-values of the stationary points of $f(x) =  x^4 - 8 x ^ 2 + 2$ and classify each point." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/example-3743.json" "file_sha256" "2408a90c9c5759e888fdec1621891586d532b8cda3c26befcf3e65418487e564" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x) = x^4 - 8 x ^ 2 + 2,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x)  = 4x^3 - 16 x,\n$$\n\nand solving $f'(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-16x & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}-4x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ x(x+2)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have stationary points at $x=0$ and $x=\\pm 2.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of $f''(x)$ at the critical points. Computing $f''(x),$ we get\n\n$$\nf''(x)= 12 x^2 - 16,\n$$\n\nand evaluating $f''(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-2) & =12(-2)^{2}-16=32>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =12(0)^{2}-16=-16<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(2) & =12(2)^{2}-16=32>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=0,$ so this is a relative maximum. On the other hand, the second derivative is positive at $x=\\pm 2,$ so these are relative minima." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/example-3743.json" "file_sha256" "2408a90c9c5759e888fdec1621891586d532b8cda3c26befcf3e65418487e564" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-21541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x)=-2{x}^{5/3}+{x}^{2/3}.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{5})=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{5})<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $x=\\frac{1}{5}$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=-2{x}^{5/3}+{x}^{2/3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{10}{3}{x}^{2/3}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-1/3}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-\\frac{20}{9}{x}^{-1/3}-\\frac{2}{9}{x}^{-4/3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{5}) & =-\\frac{20}{9}\\cdot {5}^{1/3}-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot {5}^{4/3}=-\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {5}^{1/3}<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-21541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x+16.$  Given that ${f}^{′}(-1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-1)=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Calculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x+16$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+12x+4=4(x+1)^{3}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12(x+1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ in the second derivative,   we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =12(1-1)^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find the stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+1)^{3} & =0 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point is $x=-1.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=-2,0$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-2) & =4(-2+1)^{3}=-4<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =4(0+1)^{3}=4>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the first derivative changes the sign at  $x=-1$ from minus to plus, we conclude that $x=-1$  is a local minimum\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-22164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+9.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=6x-6.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =6>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-21508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{5}+5{x}^{3}-90x+108.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(-\\sqrt{3})=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-\\sqrt{3})<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-\\sqrt{3}$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-\\sqrt{3}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $x=-\\sqrt{3}$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{5}+5{x}^{3}-90x+108,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-90.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=20{x}^{3}+30x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-\\sqrt{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-\\sqrt{3}) & =20{(-\\sqrt{3})}^{3}+30(-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =20\\cdot 3(-\\sqrt{3})+30(-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =-90\\sqrt{3}<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-21528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{7}-\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{3}+\\frac{5}{3}.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(0)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(0)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $x=0$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{7}-\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{3}+\\frac{5}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=7{x}^{6}-14{x}^{5}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=42{x}^{5}-70{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0) & =42(0)^{5}-70(0)^{4}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. Solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{x}^{6}-14{x}^{5} & =0 \\\\ 7{x}^{5}(x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=0$ and $x=2.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,1,3$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =7(-1)^{5}(-1-2)=21>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =7(1)^{5}(1-2)=-7<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =7(3)^{5}(3-2)=7\\cdot {3}^{5}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $1$ |  | $3$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nSo, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-22197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-22197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-6x+12,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-1$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(-1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify whether $x=-1$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-6x+12,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-6=6{x}^{2}-6,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ 6(x+1)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\pm 1.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=-1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=-1$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(-1)=-12<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=-1,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=-1$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-1)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=-1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-21502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=-3{x}^{5/2}+5{x}^{3/2}+15$ on $(0,\\infty ),$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=1$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify whether $x=1$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-3{x}^{5/2}+5{x}^{3/2}+15,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{3/2}+5\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}=-\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2}(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have a critical point at $x=1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}=-\\frac{45}{4}{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{4}{x}^{-1/2},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(1)=-\\frac{45}{4}(1)^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{4}(1)^{-1/2}=-\\frac{15}{2}<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=1$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-21500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2}){e}^{x},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=0$\n- ${f}^{″}(0)>0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2}){e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{x}+(-1+2x){e}^{x}=({x}^{2}+x){e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+x){e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ x(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-1,0.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=({x}^{2}+x)\\cdot {e}^{x}+(2x+1){e}^{x}=({x}^{2}+3x+1){e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =-{e}^{-1}<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =1>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I and II are true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so there is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statements III is false. $x=1$ is not a critical point.\n\n- Statement IV is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and IV only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and IV only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-114415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and IV only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+3,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(0)>0$\n- $x=0$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $x=1$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12x-12{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-12{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 12x(1-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=0,1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12-24x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0) & =12>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-12<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I and II are true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-21812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "I, III, and IV only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-21812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-2455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=3x-{x}^{3},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-1)>0$\n- $x=-1$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $x=1$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-2455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=3x-{x}^{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=3-3{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-3{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3(1-{x}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 3(1-x)(1+x) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\pm 1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-6x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =6>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-6<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I and II are true. The second derivative is positive at $x=-1,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-2455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f079d71d3b43358353afaace1454d18fd8de3091e6917d1057385bc9c55583be"} {"question" "q-2455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-2455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "I, III, and IV only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "q-2455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b08b16764c48e24d224f11c574676cb5e561bbaca21a2786aace18b0420ea16"} {"question" "e-3744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x) = x^3-6x^2-15x.$ Given that $f'(5) = 0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f''(5)  >           0$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=5$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=5$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/example-3744.json" "file_sha256" "ee17bd7030b3b511f10fe17bb2baaf4f385d32e8236cf6b0a1746ad20b833d84"} {"question" "e-3744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $x=5$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=  x^3-6x^2-15x,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x) =  3x^2-12x-15\n$$\n\nWe're given that $f'(5) = 0.$ Indeed, we can see that $f'(5) = 3(5)^2 - 12(5) - 15 = 0.$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =6x-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(5) & =6(5)-12 \\\\  & =30-12 \\\\  & =18>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/example-3744.json" "file_sha256" "ee17bd7030b3b511f10fe17bb2baaf4f385d32e8236cf6b0a1746ad20b833d84"} {"question" "e-3743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the $x$-values of the stationary points of $f(x) =  x^4 - 8 x ^ 2 + 2$ and classify each point." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/example-3743.json" "file_sha256" "2408a90c9c5759e888fdec1621891586d532b8cda3c26befcf3e65418487e564"} {"question" "e-3743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x) = x^4 - 8 x ^ 2 + 2,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x)  = 4x^3 - 16 x,\n$$\n\nand solving $f'(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-16x & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}-4x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ x(x+2)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have stationary points at $x=0$ and $x=\\pm 2.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of $f''(x)$ at the critical points. Computing $f''(x),$ we get\n\n$$\nf''(x)= 12 x^2 - 16,\n$$\n\nand evaluating $f''(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-2) & =12(-2)^{2}-16=32>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =12(0)^{2}-16=-16<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(2) & =12(2)^{2}-16=32>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=0,$ so this is a relative maximum. On the other hand, the second derivative is positive at $x=\\pm 2,$ so these are relative minima." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039650/example-3743.json" "file_sha256" "2408a90c9c5759e888fdec1621891586d532b8cda3c26befcf3e65418487e564"}] "usage" {"e-3744" [] "e-3743" [] "q-21502" [] "q-21528" [] "q-114415" []} "basis" 1377 "retractions" [[17592186064502 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nConsider the function $f(x) = x^{5} + 5x^{3} - 90x + 108$. Given that $f^{′}(-\\sqrt{3}) = 0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f^{″}(-\\sqrt{3}) < 0$\n2. $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x =-\\sqrt{3}$\n3. $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x =-\\sqrt{3}$"] [17592186064498 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFor the function $f(x) = 2x^{3} - 6x + 12$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $x =-1$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n2. $f^{″}(-1) < 0$\n3. $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x =-1$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186061603 17592186061604 17592186061605 17592186061606 17592186061607 17592186061612 17592186061613 17592186061614 17592186061615 17592186061616 17592186293836 17592186293837 17592186293838 17592186293839 17592186293840] "immutable_fields" [[17592186061602 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061602 :answer-field/id] [17592186061602 :answer-field/key] [17592186061602 :answer-field/type] [17592186061611 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061611 :answer-field/id] [17592186061611 :answer-field/key] [17592186061611 :answer-field/type] [17592186293835 :answer-field/correct] [17592186293835 :answer-field/id] [17592186293835 :answer-field/key] [17592186293835 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
